<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27290" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŭtĕus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		2. lutum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of mud</i> or <i>clay</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">defingit Rheni luteum caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 10, 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus,</span>”
				<i>of a swallow's nest</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					1, 157</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aedificium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 56, 57</span></i>
			. § 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">194: toreuma,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 4, 46, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Adam</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Cath. 3, 41</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>Bemired, muddy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gallina si sit luteis pedibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 11, 28, § 93</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Besmeared, bedaubed</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luteum ceromate corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 11, 47, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vulcanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					10, 132</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>dirty, vile,
				worthless</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">blitea et lutea meretrix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Truc. 4, 4, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">homo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 14, § 35</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">negotium,</span>”
				<i>a sorry commodity, poor affair</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 4, 14</span></i>
			, § 32.</div>
